  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Carter Center tillg&#xe5;ng till r&#xe4;ttvisa</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Carter Center Access to Justice - The Carter Center Access to Justice.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objectives of the Access to Justice (ATJ) are:
1. Improving the provision of free legal information and dispute resolution. 2. Strengthening the capacity of traditional leaders to advance good governance. 3. Supporting a policy framework to increase access to justice at a community level.
In 2014, a temporary objective was added in response to the Ebola crisis: Mobilizing chiefs and elders against Ebola</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Programmet utg&#xf6;rs av tre huvudkomponenter; att erbjuda juridisk  information och st&#xf6;d till medborgare, st&#xf6;dja konflikthantering och    governance p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5; samt att uppr&#xe4;tta och st&#xe4;rka l&#xe4;nken mellan   s&#xe5;v&#xe4;l formellt och traditionellt r&#xe4;ttstatssystem som mellan stad- och landsbygd.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program consist of three core components; provision of legal aid  support and justice information to citizens, support to dispute       resolution and good local governance and establish linkages between   formal and informal justice sectors as well as between urban and      rural areas.</narrative>
  </description>
